name: Offline audit keeps source drift partial and preserves failure causes
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART baseline
require-live-snap: 30 1 advisory findings | baseline-advisory
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 signal-only | baseline-review
submit: decision deferred Declared dependency needs owner review; runtime reachability unassessed
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | deferred-observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
ask: Does the installed offline audit produce a declared-dependency signal with a scripted deferral, without claiming runtime reachability or vulnerability execution?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare-drift
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART release
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
require-live-snap: 30 Source could not be verified | source-partial
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-after-drift
ask: Does a source-changed audit retain its usable observation as partial work and preserve the earlier decision without pretending it applies to current source?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare-failure
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART release
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
require-live-snap: 30 Owned audit adapter stopped for this fixture | failed-cause
nav-mode:
keys: /
type: Owned audit adapter
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Owned audit adapter | filtered-failure
keys: z
require-live-snap: 25 READ TRANSCRIPT | failure-reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: failure-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: failure-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: failure-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: failure-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: failure-40x12-tail
expect: PgUp/Dn
keys: PPage
live-snap: failure-40x12-page
keys: PPage
live-snap: failure-40x12-page-2
keys: PPage
live-snap: failure-40x12-cause
ask: Is the original failure cause readable through the transcript controls at six sizes, with the source warning kept separate from usable partial work?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Displayed Scan: failed | failed-report
expect: Scope: workspace history
expect: Owned audit adapter stopped for this fixture
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART report
ask: Does Report preserve failed work and its cause without turning it into a usable partial scan or complete coverage?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART stable
submit: logs
nav-mode:
keys: / Escape
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART complete
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | recovered-review
ask: Does an explicitly requested stable audit retain the earlier partial and failed history, raw observations and deferral without declaring a fix?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | restarted-review
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cargo_outcome_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: After restart without color, are two completed audits, one partial audit, one controlled failure and the retained decision readable without new work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
